## Outcome and conditions

Derive the usual large-sample variance/test bridge under the added restrictions and distinguish it from exact finite-sample inference and unsupported later corrections. All essential components listed in metadata are required. Hypothetical assessment values instantiate the checked equations; they are not historical observations or observed outcomes. Independent checks are closed-note and without hints, solution access, external retrieval or other assistance; a basic arithmetic calculator is allowed. Teach establishes and records actual help/exposure conditions before claiming independence.

## Prerequisites and checks

- [O018 outcome and repair route](../lessons/O018.md#outcome-and-conditions): the scaled-normal bridge starts from the established consistency identity.
- [O010 outcome and repair route](../lessons/O010.md#outcome-and-conditions): the classical covariance expansion/exact-distribution boundary shows what added restrictions accomplish.
- [O017 outcome and repair route](../lessons/O017.md#outcome-and-conditions): trend and unit-root distinctions delimit ordinary limit arguments.

O019-P1, item_version 1, prerequisite_diagnostic. **Prompt:** Which TS1a–3a result follows from the normalized score LLN? What covariance terms does a usual variance formula omit? Does adding a deterministic trend make a random walk weakly dependent?

**Complete key and rubric:** TS1a–3a with suitable product LLNs and nonsingular Q gives consistency. Serial error covariance terms are omitted by the usual no-serial-correlation formula, distinct from mere weak dependence. A deterministic trend does not remove accumulated random-walk innovations. Require all clauses; repair O018 consistency, O010 full covariance expansion, O017 persistence. Pass requires every requested reason and result; partial for an omitted reason or unresolved isolated arithmetic slip; fail for the conflicting mechanism. This diagnostic never counts as acquisition. Current or explicitly compatible committed independent prerequisite evidence may permit skipping its check; familiarity alone cannot. Use the cited complete prerequisite lesson or the named included foundation, then the worked example, after a partial/failing entry check.

