## Rubric and independence

Required components: scaled_score_clt_and_variance_calculation, additional_error_restrictions_and_failure_consequences, exact_vs_asymptotic_normality_trend_and_scope_limits. Each full prompt/key below elicits every component; all are necessary for a pass on every permitted pair. Accept algebraically equivalent expressions and clearly defined opposite cash-flow signs with correct interpretation. A pass requires all requested outputs/reasons, correct units/assumptions and no critical conceptual error. Partial means a missing component or an unresolved isolated arithmetic slip with an otherwise valid method; independent correction is required for a pass. Fail means a critical mechanism/condition is wrong. Unscorable means a response or its help/exposure conditions cannot be established. Unknown help conditions are never independent evidence.

Critical errors: Consistency asserted to guarantee usual standard errors; weak dependence equated with serially uncorrelated errors; asymptotic statistic claimed exact Student without strong assumptions; universal efficiency or unit-root cure asserted.

Acquisition requires two distinct unused unassisted full checks selected from the six exact metadata routes. Every I/D form covers all components; W1, S1, the prerequisite and C1 are forbidden substitutes. A D form used for acquisition cannot later be counted again as delayed success. No teach-generated item may replace a named full check; additional verified explanation/practice is allowed under the unchanged method and may not fabricate evidence. If fewer than two fresh forms remain for acquisition, return a plan_issue for an additional prepared bank.

