## Misconceptions and correction

An observed omitted term/sign is tentative until the learner explains it; compare the reasoning with the critical errors above. Score the original response before providing help. Route a conceptual failure to the relevant included derivation and prerequisite, then use an unused full form.

O019-C1, item_version 1, narrow_correction. **Prompt:** Serial error correlation violates TS5a while the consistency assumptions remain valid. Must OLS lose consistency, and are ordinary standard errors still justified? **Key/rubric:** Consistency may remain under TS1a–3a, but the usual variance guarantee fails because relevant error cross products contribute covariance terms. A different valid inference method needs separate preparation; no automatic correction is assumed. Pass requires all keyed reasoning; partial for a missing part; fail for the conflicting mechanism. This repairs a common inference only; it cannot substitute for a full numerical/capability check.

Give at most two hints (first identify the date/unit, second point to the included identity); after ineffective hints show the relevant worked step. After two unsuccessful independent attempts stop repeated quizzing, revisit the explanation/prerequisite and preserve the unresolved status.

